; A member reached through a VALUE needs no `use` of the value's type
; (2026-10-09): `c.helpers.y` with the record holding `helpers` used and the
; helpers' own concept not. `use` makes a name WRITABLE -- an annotation, a
; construction, a static call --; a value brings its type along, and its
; methods and fields are found whether or not this file names the type.
;
; Until that day this was refused (`member y of EmitHelpers: the concept is
; not visible in this file`, 2026-09-24; before THAT the emitter aborted,
; rc 16, no file and no line). The refusal could not stand once two packages'
; records of one name were two types: a program cannot `use` both, so a
; method on the second was unwritable. A LIBRARY root: a library's modules
; are where the visibility gate bites.
; args: --no-prelude
; expect-ir: %y = extractvalue %_Z11EmitHelpers %helpers, 1
define member_of_unused_type
{
    module helpers
    module ctx
    module user
}
